# Everything text is LF in the index. A CRLF shebang is "bad interpreter" on
# Linux, and every line of this repo runs on a Pi.
#
# This started as `*.sh text eol=lf`, written after an editor pass normalised
# install.sh to CRLF. That rule was too narrow: it keys on the extension, and
# the one script with no extension -- scripts/skylapse-admin, which every
# privileged operation goes through -- was not matched. It shipped with a
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` shebang in 0.5.4, so restart-services exited 127, the
# updater read that as a bad build, and two releases rolled themselves back
# with no way to see why. Match everything instead of guessing at names.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git should not touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.gz  binary
*.xz  binary
*.dng binary
